---
// Static figure: three works measured against one standing person, all three panels at one scale (1 unit = 5 cm,
// ground at y 112). Left, the Gubbio studiolo in section (485 cm high, 518 cm wide) with the eye line its intarsia is
// set out for (66 in. ≈ 168 cm, after Daniel Kershaw's account for the Metropolitan Museum). Middle, a ci wara crest
// (the Met's 2016.574 is 76.2 cm high) worn on top of the head over a fibre costume. Right, an inrō set at the waist
// (the case is 8.4 cm high), with an enlarged view of how netsuke, cord, bead and case hang from the sash. Simple
// drawings of size relations, not reconstructions; the person and the costume are generic. Uses the step layout of the
// stained-glass figure, in three columns.
---
<figure class="glass-steps three">
  <ol>
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 160 120" aria-hidden="true">
        <path class="bs-room" d="M28 15 H132 V112 H28 Z" />
        <path class="bs-panel" d="M32 77 H128 M32 97 H128" />
        <path class="lv-sight" d="M58 78.5 H130" />
        <circle class="lv-person" cx="56" cy="78.5" r="3" />
        <path class="lv-person-line" d="M56 81.5 V97 M56 97 L52 112 M56 97 L60 112 M56 85 L51 95 M56 85 L61 95" />
        <path class="lv-ground" d="M0 112 H160" />
      </svg>
      <p><strong>走进去：一间房</strong>书房高 4.85 米、宽 5.18 米，人站在里面只占它的三分之一高。镶嵌出来的柜子、长凳和影子，都按地面以上约 168 厘米（66 英寸）的视平线来安排（虚线）。</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 160 120" aria-hidden="true">
        <path class="bs-fibre" d="M70 76 L66 106 M73 76 L70 107 M76 76 L74 107 M79 76 L79 107 M82 76 L84 107 M85 76 L88 107 M88 76 L92 106 M72 90 L68 104 M86 90 L90 104" />
        <path class="bs-crest" d="M78 72 C76.5 67 75.5 63 75 58 M80.5 72 C80 67 80 63 80.5 58 M75.5 75 L78 72 L80.5 72 L83 75" />
        <circle class="lv-person" cx="79" cy="78" r="3" />
        <path class="lv-person-line" d="M79 106 L76 112 M79 106 L82 112" />
        <path class="bs-staff" d="M95 82 L97 112" />
        <path class="lv-ground" d="M0 112 H160" />
      </svg>
      <p><strong>戴起来：头顶上的雕刻</strong>契瓦拉头饰高约 76 厘米，固定在舞者的头顶，舞者全身披着长长的纤维服装。人们看到的，是一个比人高出一截、会动的形象。</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 160 120" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle class="lv-person" cx="40" cy="78.5" r="3" />
        <path class="lv-person-line" d="M40 81.5 V97 M40 97 L36 112 M40 97 L44 112 M40 85 L35 95 M40 85 L45 95" />
        <path class="bs-sash" d="M37 92 H43" />
        <rect class="bs-inro" x="42.4" y="93" width="1.2" height="1.7" />
        <path class="bs-lead" d="M44.5 93.5 L88 66" />
        <circle class="bs-lens" cx="112" cy="58" r="34" />
        <rect class="bs-sash-big" x="80" y="36" width="64" height="12" />
        <rect class="bs-netsuke" x="104" y="26" width="13" height="10" rx="3" />
        <path class="bs-cord" d="M110.5 36 V58" />
        <circle class="bs-ojime" cx="110.5" cy="60.5" r="2.6" />
        <rect class="bs-inro" x="102" y="63" width="17" height="22" rx="4" />
        <path class="lv-ground" d="M0 112 H160" />
      </svg>
      <p><strong>挂在腰间：手掌里的东西</strong>印笼只有 8.4 厘米高，在人身上只是腰间的一个小点（右边是放大的样子）。根付卡在腰带上方，绳子从腰带后面穿下去，吊起珠子和印笼。</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption>示意图：三个画面用同一个比例尺，人约 1.8 米高，依据大都会艺术博物馆公布的尺寸绘制；放大圈不按比例。人物、服装和房间里的陈设都只是示意，不是对原来情形的复原。</figcaption>
</figure>
